# Release-archive hygiene.
#
# `.council/` is tracked engineering/research history (MCP history dumps, raw
# RPC responses, captured response headers, generated images). It is useful in
# the developer repository but must never ship in a release artifact produced
# by `git archive`. Both patterns are intentional: the first excludes the
# directory entry itself, the second guarantees every nested path is excluded
# (gitattributes does not treat a trailing-slash pattern as recursive).
/.council export-ignore
/.council/** export-ignore
